# adpcm_ima — IMA/DVI ADPCM, the scheme WAV calls format 0x11 and AVI
# carries beside MJPEG. Four bits a sample, fixed rate, 4:1.
#
# Three modules. `adpcm_ima_enc` is the encoder and is `top`;
# `adpcm_ima_dec` is its peer and not a dependency of it; `adpcm_step`
# is the 89-entry step table both of them look up, in a module of its
# own because this flow has no include mechanism and a table copied
# into two files is two tables.
#
# **The two halves are not verified the same way, because they are not
# specified the same way.** What a decoder does with a nibble is fixed
# and `adpcm_ima_dec` is checked sample for sample against ffmpeg's
# decoder; which nibble an encoder picks is a choice, and
# `adpcm_ima_enc` is checked by round trip — ffmpeg's decoder must
# rebuild exactly the predictor sequence the encoder said it would.
# `ip/audio/adpcm_ima/README.md` §"Against ffmpeg" has both, and the
# measurement of where the two encoders differ.
name adpcm_ima
version 1.0.0
license MIT
description "IMA/DVI ADPCM encoder and decoder: four bits a sample at a fixed 4:1, the 89-step table shared, with the predictor and step index a WAV block header carries brought out"

top adpcm_ima_enc
target ice40
target ecp5
target xc7

source rtl/adpcm_step.v
source rtl/adpcm_ima_enc.v
source rtl/adpcm_ima_dec.v

port clk in
port rst_n in
port load in
port load_pred in 16
port load_index in 7
port in_sample in 16
port in_valid in
port in_ready out
port out_nibble out 4
port out_valid out
port out_ready in
port predictor out 16
port step_index out 7
